w: On a hill far a- way stood an old rug- ged cross, The * em- blem of suf- f'ring and shame; *
w: Oh, that old rug- ged cross, so de- spised by the world, Has a won- drous at- trac- tion for me; *
w: In that old rug- ged cross, stained with blood so di- vine, A * won- * drous beau- ty I see, *
w: To the old rug- ged cross I will ev- er be true; Its * shame and re- proach glad- ly bear; *
